 # Xonix Runtime Maintainer
 
+For [narrow HUD layout](../../../docs/narrow-hud-layout.md), reflow complete values
+and glyphs while preserving Large text, DOM order, 44-pixel targets and the
+existing arena fitter. Do not repair intrinsic overflow with cropping, font
+reduction or canvas/simulation changes. Verify actual browser bounds through
+narrow-to-wide-to-narrow resize and both text faces; finite host rectangles do
+not prove CSS fit. Preserve the 20-case HUD matrix and ten native keyboard Pause
+checks as separate local evidence, including corrected stale captures and the
+original Solo outline failure. Keep the Pause indicator inside its unchanged
+target; defensive `.controller-focus` styling does not make Solo Pause a menu
+navigation target. Maximum-value fixtures and physical/integrated/public gates
+remain open. Use the guide's scoped regression and authoring example.
+
 Current sequencing is [the revised whole-game UX plan](../../../docs/whole-game-ux-plan.md). Settings is a host-local surface with shared Controls, Audio, Appearance & accessibility and Game data categories. Use `attachSettingsPanels` for categories and compose `settingsTabOwnsKey` into the host navigation capture boundary; never add a second preference or controller owner. Enter the real category before editing or asserting control reachability. Preserve input release, paused checkpoints, actual opener return, retained category and explicit Resume. Team Settings is a native dialog, not an Options disclosure; model native Tab/default cancel locally in host fixtures without inventing application return focus. Quick Sound controls operate the existing master authority; their visible labels and pressed state agree across modes.
 
 Menu/audio `pageshow.persisted` reconciliation reads validated current storage and preserves unsaved/session-only local intent. Storage reads, listeners and dialog close callbacks can retire their owner or produce newer intent. Recheck ownership before writes/focus; terminal cleanup retires before closing native surfaces. Test late audio activation after mute, stale restoration, failed saves and actual browser Back separately. A cold Back page load is not BFCache proof. Interface appearance does not pin a complete game theme or change existing map/art identity; exact complete-theme restoration remains a later qualified contract.
diff --git a/game/couch/couch.css b/game/couch/couch.css
index 8f4618ecb..d4a2e3996 100644
--- a/game/couch/couch.css
+++ b/game/couch/couch.css
@@ -418,6 +418,30 @@ body.race-focus #couch-app {
     font-size: 23px;
   }
 }
+/* Reflow the HUD before its intrinsic width can widen both fitted arenas.
+   Pause, series score and clock keep their DOM order and existing type sizes. */
+@media (max-width: 320px) {
+  body.race-focus #couch-app {
+    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
+  }
+  .race-hud {
+    display: grid;
+    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
+    row-gap: 6px;
+  }
+  #race-pause {
+    grid-column: 1 / -1;
+    justify-self: start;
+    white-space: nowrap;
+  }
+  .race-score {
+    min-width: 0;
+    justify-self: start;
+  }
+  #race-clock {
+    justify-self: end;
+  }
+}
